    <DataNode elementId="AT1G23740-MONOMER" textLabel="alkenal/one oxidoreductase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZUC1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">AOR is an alkenal/one oxidoreductase that acts on compounds with unsaturated &amp;alpha;&amp;beta;-carbonyls. The activity of this enzyme with a number of substrates was demonstrated &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; using a truncated form of the protein that lacked approximately 80 of the first amino acids. This portion of the protein is variable between family members and likely encodes an N-terminal transit peptide for directing AOR to the chloroplast. AOR shows a preference for reducing the double bonds in small carbonyl compounds, especially in &amp;alpha;&amp;beta;-unsaturated ketones |CITS: [21169366][18633119]|. AOR likely plays a role in detoxifying reactive carbonyls formed during lipid peroxidation to help protect the photosynthetic process |CITS: [21169366]|. Although it can act on a number of the short chain carbonyls that might damage biomolecules, such as |FRAME: ACETOIN acetoin| and |FRAME: CPD-13222 &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-4-hexen-3-one|, it does not act on a number of other compounds, such as |FRAME: TRANS-2-HEXENAL trans-2-hexenal|, which must be detoxified by other enzymes, such as |FRAME: AT2G37770-MONOMER ChlAKR| and |FRAME: AT1G54870-MONOMER ChlADR| |CITS: [21169366]|. Arabidopsis possesses an enzyme with some overlapping actvity, |FRAME: AT5G16970 AtAER|, but, it belongs to a different tree in the medium-chain dehydrogenase / reductase superfamily and it localizes to the cytosol and nucleus |CITS: [21169366][16299173]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G23740-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G23740.1" />
